---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../components/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="About Chekpoint.gg" variant="centered">
  <div class="about-page">
    <div class="about-header">
      <a href="/" class="back-link">← Chekpoint</a>
      <h1>About</h1>
    </div>

    <div class="about-section">
      <h2>What is Chekpoint?</h2>
      <p>Chekpoint is a game review site built by two people who wanted a better place to talk about games online. Sam and Bill started the project because nothing quite fit -- something between the structure of Metacritic and the noise of Reddit was missing. So they built it themselves.</p>
      <p>The core idea is simple. Score games, write about them, follow people whose taste you trust, and see where your opinions land compared to everyone else's. You can browse everything without an account. To write reviews and participate in the community you'll need to sign up, which takes about a minute and is free.</p>
      <p>Groups are a big part of what makes Chekpoint a little different. Create or join one with friends, keep a shared watchlist, log gaming sessions, and track what everyone has been playing. Public groups are open to anyone. Private groups are invite-only.</p>
      <p>Chekpoint is not affiliated with any publisher, studio, or platform. No sponsored content, no monetization. Just a side project that got a little out of hand.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
      <h2 class="faq-heading">FAQ</h2>

      <div class="faq-list">
        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Do I need an account to use Chekpoint?</h3>
          <p>You can browse reviews, game pages, and profiles without signing up. An account lets you write reviews, follow other users, build a watchlist, and join groups.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Does it cost anything?</h3>
          <p>No. Chekpoint is free to use.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How is a game's score calculated?</h3>
          <p>Each reviewer gives a game a score from 0.1 to 10. The score shown on a game's page is the average of all published reviews for that game.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can I edit or delete a review after posting?</h3>
          <p>Yes to both. You can edit or delete any of your reviews from the review page or your profile.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What is a hot take?</h3>
          <p>A hot take is a review where your score diverges significantly from what everyone else gave a game. If the community averages an 8 and you give it a 2, that qualifies. The Hot Takes page surfaces those outlier reviews.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>What are groups?</h3>
          <p>Groups are shared spaces for you and other users. Members share a watchlist, can log gaming sessions together, and track what everyone has been playing. Groups can be public or private.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How do I join a group?</h3>
          <p>Public groups can be joined directly from the groups page. Private groups require an invite link or a join request that a group admin approves.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can I review a game I haven't finished?</h3>
          <p>Yes, and we think you should. A lot of games don't have a real ending, and a lot of people have hundreds of hours in something they would never call complete. If you have a genuine opinion, write about it.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Can I get notified when someone I follow posts?</h3>
          <p>Yes. When you follow someone you can toggle notifications on for their account so you hear about new reviews when they post.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How do I report a review?</h3>
          <p>There is a report option in the "..." menu on any review. We review reports manually and take action when something violates the community guidelines.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>How do I close my account?</h3>
          <p>Fill out the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> and we will take care of it. We are working on adding account deletion directly from the settings page.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
          <h3>Is there a mobile app?</h3>
          <p>Not currently. Chekpoint is web-only, but it works on mobile.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 680px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 40px;
  }

  .about-header {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .back-link {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
    transition: color 0.15s;
  }
  .back-link:hover { color: var(--text-primary); }

  h1 {
    font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
    font-size: 32px;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .about-section {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    padding: 36px 40px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
  }

  .about-section h2 {
    font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 4px;
  }

  .faq-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .faq-heading {
    font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .faq-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 16px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .faq-item {
    padding: 24px 32px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg-card);
  }
  .faq-item:last-child { border-bottom: none; }

  h3 {
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text-primary);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  p {
    font-size: 14px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  a { color: var(--accent); }
  a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .about-section { padding: 24px 20px; }
    .faq-item { padding: 20px; }
    h1 { font-size: 26px; }
  }
</style>
